{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"wjsekfghks"},"story_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["browser","agent"],"value":"Hi, we're Mikkel and Paul, and we're building gitdot, an open-source alternative to GitHub.<p>We started gitdot because GitHub annoyed us. Turns out GitHub is genuinely complex, and getting the fundamentals right is harder than it looks. So we threw out most of our roadmap and shipped the smallest thing we'd actually be proud of.<p>What’s shipping today:<p>- Accounts, public and private repos, and public orgs<p>- <em>Browse</em> repos and users on the web (with a few keyboard shortcuts for fun)<p>- Push over smart HTTP (auth via our CLI)<p>- One click import your GitHub repositories to gitdot<p>It's not fully usable yet as issues, pull requests, and CI <em>aren't</em> built. But we wanted to show what we have and get early feedback. Take a look and let us know what you think."},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Show HN: gitdot – a GitHub alternative built in Rust"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://gitdot.io"}}

